 "summary": "GitHub PR Guardian is an AI‑augmented code review tool that scans diffs for secrets, unsafe patterns and dependency issues, then uses Gemini to generate a structured review. The implementation is functional but has high‑complexity functions, incomplete guardrails and limited testing.",
 "strengths": [
  "Clear modular layout separating diff parsing, static scanning, LLM client and reporting.",
  "Comprehensive README with usage examples and feature description.",
  "Static rule scanner and Gemini client are implemented and integrated."
 ],
 "top_fixes": [
  "Refactor large functions (e.g., parse_unified_diff, main, _execute_pipeline) to reduce cyclomatic complexity below 10.",
  "Add proper exception chaining (raise ... from err) and avoid silent except blocks.",
  "Enforce token/step limits and timeout handling around Gemini API calls."
 ],
